"hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1123,"Muhammad ibn Bashar, Amr ibn Ali, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas narrated to us. Muhammad ibn Amr said: Ghandar narrated to us, and he said The other two: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Bundar said, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Warqa’, and the other two said: On the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Warqa’, On the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “When the establishment of prayer is performed, there is no prayer except “The written.” Yaqoub Al-Dawraqi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, Amr bin Dinar told us, he said: I heard Ata’ Ibn Yasar says: On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example."
1124,"Salam bin Junada al-Qurashi told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Salih bin Rustum, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: And why I was praying the two rak’ahs, and he saw me praying them, so he discouraged me, so he pulled me away, the prayer was performed, and he said: “Do you want to pray four rak’ahs in the morning?” It was said to Abu Amer, meaning Saleh bin Rustum: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes. Abu Ammar told us: Al-Nadr bin Shumayl told us, on the authority of Abu Amir, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The prayer was established, so I stood up I prayed two rak'ahs, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pulled me in and said: ""Should I pray four rak'ahs in the morning?"""
1125,"Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli told us, Hammad told us, meaning Ibn Zaid, h. Ahmad bin Abdah told us, he said: Abbad told us, meaning Ibn Abbad Al-Muhallabi, H. Ahmad Ibn Abdah narrated to us, also on the authority of Abd Al-Wahid Ibn Ziyad, H. Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abd Allah narrated to us Yazid Al-Muqri, we are told by Al-Fazari, meaning Marwan bin Muawiyah, Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Bundar told us, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, and Muhammad bin Yahya al-Quti’ told us, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Shu’bah told us, All of them on the authority of Asim, meaning the one who is cross-eyed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, who said: A man came while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was performing the morning prayer, so he kneeled down. Two rak'ahs, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished his prayer, he said: ""O so-and-so, which one is your prayer, the one you prayed with us or the one you prayed with?"" For yourself.” This is the wording of the hadith of Hammad bin Zayd."
1126,"Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi narrated to us strange news. He said: Muhammad bin Ammar, meaning Al-Ansari, narrated to us on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah, who is the son of Abu Nimr, on the authority of Anas, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out when prayer was established and saw people praying two rak’ahs with a wheel, so he said: ‘Two prayers. Together, he forbade praying in the mosque if the prayer was established.” Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Anas, similar to his saying: “Two prayers together,” and nothing more than this. Muhammad bin Ishaq said: He narrated this. The news is from Malik bin Anas, and Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Sharik bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, mursal, and Ibrahim bin Tahman narrated, on the authority of He is a partner with both reports, on the authority of Anas, and on the authority of Abu Salamah, both of them were narrated to us by Muhammad bin Aqeel, by Hafs bin Abdullah, to us by Ibrahim bin. Tahman reported with both chains of transmission separately, Anas reported separately, and Ibn Salamah reported separately."
